</surname> <given-names>SJ</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Bai</surname> <given-names>GH</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Chae</surname> <given-names>GT</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Identification of mycobacterial species by comparative sequence analysis of the RNA polymerase gene (<italic>rpoB</italic>).</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source> <year>1999</year>;<volume>37</volume>:<fpage>1714</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>20</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10325313</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R9"><label>9. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Adekambi</surname> <given-names>T</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Berger</surname> <given-names>P</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Raoult</surname> <given-names>D</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Drancourt</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name> <article-title>rpoB gene sequence-based characterization of emerging non-tuberculous mycobacteria with descriptions of <italic>Mycobacterium bolletii</italic> sp. nov., <italic>Mycobacterium phocaicum</italic> sp. nov. and <italic>Mycobacterium aubagnense</italic> sp. nov.</article-title><source>Int J Syst Evol Microbiol</source> <year>2006</year>;<volume>56</volume>:<fpage>133</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>43</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1099/ijs.0.63969-0</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16403878</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R10"><label>10. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Ad&#x000e9;kambi</surname> <given-names>T</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Stein</surname> <given-names>A</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Carvajal</surname> <given-names>J</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Raoult</surname> <given-names>D</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Drancourt</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Description of <italic>Mycobacterium conceptionense</italic> sp. nov., a <italic>Mycobacterium fortuitum</italic> group organism isolated from a posttraumatic osteitis inflammation.</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source> <year>2006</year>;<volume>44</volume>:<fpage>1268</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>73</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/JCM.44.4.1268-1273.2006</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16597850</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>